# Agent Loop Rule

This workflow is not active by default in the starter template. Copy this file into `.cursor/rules/` only if the project intentionally adopts an autonomous workplan loop.

When `optional/agent-loop/ACTIVE_WORKPLAN.md` is adapted into the project and an active run log exists, use them as the source of truth for ongoing implementation work.

## Default Behavior

When the user asks to build, implement, continue, test, QA, refactor, scaffold, or execute a plan:

1. Read the active workplan.
2. Read the run log.
3. Identify the next unchecked task.
4. Execute that task.
5. Run relevant validation.
6. Fix clear in-scope failures.
7. Update the workplan.
8. Update the run log.
9. Continue until complete or blocked.

## Stop Conditions

Stop and ask the user if a task requires secrets, production data, real charges, real user messages, production deployment, destructive actions, ambiguous business logic, repeated failures, or risky architecture changes.

## Reporting

Report what was completed, validation results, what remains, blockers, and the next recommended task. Do not claim a command passed unless it actually ran and passed.
